  "paper_id": "ccs-2023-on-the-security-of-kzg-commitment-for-vss-e4b6cf31",
  "title": "On the Security of KZG Commitment for VSS",
  "abstract": "The constant-sized polynomial commitment scheme by Kate, Zaverucha, and Goldberg (Asiscrypt 2010), also known as the KZG commitment, is an essential component in designing bandwidth-efficient verifiable secret-sharing (VSS) protocols. We point out, however, that the KZG commitment is missing two important properties that are crucial for VSS protocols.",
